Turns off both fixes for a want stranded by hash mismatches (DESIGN.md
§7.5), which this pin needs together because either one alone still
rescues the file. Draft 31's events (commit 2cacad7) go back to the pre-fix
code: a batch announcing the wanted content (`note_announced`) and a source
reconnecting (`PeerConnected`) release nothing. Draft 32's expiry (commit
7a62e61) is off as well: `expire` releases no exclusion and `next_deadline`
asks for no wake-up for one. A source excluded after a mismatch, and a want
that gave up after two, then stay so until the index at the path changes.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_want_that_gave_up_is_wanted_again

